## Context
Child of 1102. Implement a project-scoped one-way migration helper for memory/DREAM.md -> memory/HOARD.md and memory/dreams/ -> memory/hoards/. Preflight conflicts, unreadable inputs and filesystem indirection before writes; dry-run writes nothing; repeat is a no-op. Preserve journal/report bytes and provenance, update active reference/link targets, and give migrated prompt a new revision. Do not activate the rename yet.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Behavioral fixtures cover fresh new format, old linked reports, repeated invocation, dry-run, both coexistence conflicts, dangling/external symlinks and unreadable inputs; verify byte/provenance preservation. Full make check passes.

## Raid Imagine and Plan — 2026-10-15
Implement scripts/hoard_migrate.py with importable plan_migration/apply_migration and a PROJECT [--dry-run] [--reference RELATIVE_PATH ...] CLI. Stdlib suffices: filesystem moves and selected text reference edits, no dependency/framework needed. Caller owns isolated Git branch; helper never mutates Git. Default references: prompt, current index and topics; explicitly inventory additional active reference files. Preserve report/journal/ciphertext bytes and historical ledgers. Preflight all coexistence/unreadable/path/symlink conflicts before writes, stage edits, refuse intervening changes, recover originals on ordinary write failures and report any residual error. Advance migrated prompt revision once. No recursive cross-project sweep or blanket historical substitution.
First tests: real temporary old/new project fixtures with linked reports; dry-run and repeat compare complete tree bytes; conflicts/unreadable/dangling/external links leave both project and outside sentinel unchanged. Include meaningful rollback fault injection. Paths: helper, behavioral test, own ticket (plus common raid annotations in initial base). Gates: affected pytest, make check-fast, make lint, full make check. Antipattern: no new wording-only ratchets or generic migration framework.

## Raid feasibility — 2026-10-15
PASS: helper and behavioral test paths new; stdlib sufficient. Nine paths including seven common preparation tickets, no registry changes or wave conflicts. Reject explicit immutable-history references; verify unreadability at real/simulated I/O boundary rather than mode-bit inference. Ordinary failures require rollback/residual reporting; no claim of crash-atomic multi-file transactions.
